cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Implementation of the BFSC cylinder finite element
type: software
abstract: >-
  The `bfsccylinder` module implements the single-curvature BFSC (SC-BFSC)
  finite element of cylindrical shells, for linear and nonlinear analyses,
  with Donnell-type and Sanders-Koiter type kinematics. It computes the
  contributions of each element to:

  * The linear constitutive stiffness matrix, for linear static analyses

  * The geometric stiffness matrix, for linear buckling analyses

  * The mass matrix, for natural frequency analyses

  * The internal force vector and the tangent stiffness matrix, for
    geometrically nonlinear static analyses

  * The force vector and the unsymmetric load stiffness matrix of a
    follower pressure, normal to the deformed mid-surface, for nonlinear
    static and linear buckling analyses
message: >-
  Please, cite this software using:
  Saullo G. P. Castro (2026). Implementation of the BFSC cylinder finite element (Version 0.7.0). https://github.com/saullocastro/bfsccylinder.
